  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Comfortable and dry to end July \nRefreshing northerly breeze and uptick in daytime stratocu \nproviding another Fall-ish type day for late July across CPA. \nStill can't rule out a brief and negligible shower/sprinkle \nrotating around the backside of the departing upper level low\nacross the eastern periphery of the CWA; however the majority of\nthe area will hold onto dry weather to close out the month.  \n\nClearing skies expected tonight with decreasing wind as high \npressure slides eastward from the Ohio Valley. Areas of fog are \nlikely to develop in the valleys across the west-central\nAlleghenies with min temps in the 50-60F range into early \nFriday morning. Comfortably warm and dry end to July on Friday \nwith a mix of sun and clouds and max temps in the low to mid\n80s.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Rain most likely Sunday with increased risk of \nflooding downpours \n\nAn axis of anomalous PW ~1.5\" along and ahead of an approaching\ncold front combined with favorable upper dynamics should support\nactive convection reaching CPA as early as late Saturday night\nwith max POPs centered on the 24hr Sunday window. With some\npotential for training in the moist low level SW flow parallel\nto the front and increased vulnerability given recent very heavy\nrainfall, WPC introduced a level 2/4 excessive rain outlook\n(ERO) that covers much of north central PA. Exact timing and\nplacement of max QPF remains a bit unclear as there is still\nsome model differences regarding the evolution of the upper \ntrough.",
